before joining the team the  silver sniper's experience with video  games  generally was very limited but under the  tutelage of former pro player  tommy potty ingamarsen they eagerly  began to pick up the basics of  counter-strike  i was here many times everybody  was still and many times before  it's possible to win if you lose you can  teach yourself about your mistakes  and their efforts paid dividends with  the team  finding themselves comfortable enough to  compete in lan events by the end of 2017  and although silverware did evade their  grasp that year  the team was motivated enough by their  progress that they  ramped up their practice schedule and by  the spring of 2018  the silver snipers found themselves  competing for their first  trophy against an opponent that would  later become their greatest  rival finland's grey gunners  and it was in that grandpa final i mean  i mean grand finals  that the silver sniper showed everyone  just how deadly they could be  coming from the crosstalk time he  gets a nice nice heads up for the d  slayer but then  windy the team captain takes the round  for the swedes  fights finger  waiting on the side and gets down the  clutch 10  12.  the jerry tries to shoot through the  barrels  ah just a few pixels  to the right and trigger finger gets  down dirty hurry  after a thrilling two maps the silver  snipers emerged victorious  claiming their first senior cs title  and they were as excited as you can  imagine  [Applause]  now unfortunately for the silver snipers  the grey gunners would exact their  revenge at dreamhack summer 2018 but  in spite of falling short against their  finnish rivals  the lovable swedes really made a splash  in the scene  long after that event the team's lineup  went through a slight shuffleboard  sorry shuffle joining knitting knight  trigger finger  windy and die hard birdie was balthazar  el nino aguirre  who discovered his passion for cs go  through  playing with his son alongside their new  rifler  frederick jagarne anderson stepped in as  the team's coach  and with his support the snipers doubled  their efforts to challenge  yet again for another world championship  and by the time  dreamhack rolled around again in 2019  they had their chance once again the  snipers found themselves  facing off against their rivals the grey  gunners  in the grand finals the stage was set  the pressure was on  and the stakes were high and when these  two ancient juggernauts went at it  they gave fans what has to be the  greatest  spectacle in senior esports history  hey  this is weird  [Music]  so  counter terrorism  now as exciting as becoming the cs go  senior world champions  was for the silver snipers it's their  journey to  that moment that they truly hold dear  for the team's oldest member  die hard birdie counter-strike has  become more than just a hobby that he  indulges in for a few hours a day  it's become an opportunity for him to  bond with his family  i love playing with my dad and sometimes  my daughter gets involved so all three  of us play  my 12 year old daughter me and my dad  and while birdie has  officially stepped away from the  competitive scene like all  true esports retirees he's decided to  focus on growing his twitch channel  let's dance  as for the rest of the silver snipers  they continue to practice together  and show no signs of slowing down and  they've even begun fixing their sights  on zoomers so watch out i'll battle any  gamer  too scared kiss my own  look while it's very easy to write off  seniors gaming as a gimmick  it's really important to remember where  the idea for the silver snipers came  from  age can be the ultimate obstacle when it  comes to finding ways to  socialize with others loneliness and  depression are a  very real problem among seniors it's  easy for the older generation to feel  like the world has moved on without them  especially when they see their grandkids  glued to screens and seemingly getting  all the socializing they need from that  on top of the obvious social  and mental health benefits that gaming  offers  it's also been shown to improve focus  decision-making abilities  and problem-solving skills for those who  choose to spend their time  playing and for the silver snipers the  rush of defusing a bomb after clutching  a tight round  simply can't be beat you feel exciting  you feel blood pressure  you feel everything and sure it might be  difficult to get  graham and gramps to help you reach  global elite but  thanks to the silver snipers there's far  less reason to dismiss  the possibility of getting older  generations interested in esports  while most seniors are hesitant when it  comes to giving things like video games  a chance  these feisty fragging fogies have proven  that with some help from your loved ones  even learning to play a game as daunting  as cs go  is a challenge that can be overcome i  like to say  for the old people just find some guts  to wake up the spirits and ask  your children or grandchildren to help  you  this is very good for coordination  communication  between all generations and this dogged  determination and resilient competitive  spirit  is what makes rosters like the silver  snipers and grey gunners  trailblazing heroes not only are they  showing their fellow senior citizens  that they can  enjoy some of the things the modern age  has to offer but they found a way to  connect with a world that they  increasingly felt they weren't a part of  i mean i think this has been  really a life-changing experience for  them and  not only have they learned to love and  embrace technology  but i think they've also seen what  technology can do for them  and honestly as a future old person  how could you not love that  what about silver snipers that's not top  five i don't think we have a good top  five i think they would still dumpster  us  oh my literally three of them snipers  damn it if we took like four rounds off  these guys  i would be i would be impressed i'll be  honest we have zero utility with zero  all we can do is just hop out of palace  and just  line it straight for ct okay  no and then we're gonna go b let's go  what what you just killed our coach

